exercises.instructions:
Write a function called `groupByDecade` that takes an array of movie objects and returns an object where keys are decade strings (e.g., `"1990s"`) and values are arrays of movie titles from that decade.

Example:
```
groupByDecade(movies)
// Returns: { "1970s": ["The Codfather"], "1980s": ["The Whining"], "1990s": [...], ... }
```

exercises.starterCode:
/**
 * @param {Object[]} movies - Array of movie objects
 * @returns {Object} Object mapping decade strings to arrays of titles
 */
function groupByDecade(movies) {

}

exercises.solution:
function groupByDecade(movies) {
  return movies.reduce((acc, movie) => {
    const decade = Math.floor(movie.year / 10) * 10 + 's';
    if (!acc[decade]) acc[decade] = [];
    acc[decade].push(movie.title);
    return acc;
  }, {});
}

