exercises.instructions:
Create a function called `directorFilmography` that takes an array of movie objects and returns an object where each key is a director's name and each value is an object containing:
- `movies`: array of `{ title, year, imdbRating }` objects sorted by year
- `avgRating`: average IMDB rating of their movies (rounded to 1 decimal)

Example:
```
directorFilmography(movies)
// Returns: {
//   "Frank Darabonk": {
//     movies: [{ title: "The Shawshank Exemption", year: 1994, imdbRating: 9.3 }],
//     avgRating: 9.3
//   },
//   ...
// }
```

exercises.solution:
function directorFilmography(movies) {
  const filmography = movies.reduce((acc, movie) => {
    const name = movie.director.name;
    if (!acc[name]) acc[name] = { movies: [], totalRating: 0 };
    acc[name].movies.push({ title: movie.title, year: movie.year, imdbRating: movie.ratings.imdb });
    acc[name].totalRating += movie.ratings.imdb;
    return acc;
  }, {});

  const result = {};
  for (const [name, data] of Object.entries(filmography)) {
    result[name] = {
      movies: data.movies.sort((a, b) => a.year - b.year),
      avgRating: Math.round(data.totalRating / data.movies.length * 10) / 10
    };
  }
  return result;
}

