exercises.instructions:
Create a function called `genreReport` that takes an array of movie objects and returns an object where each key is a genre and each value is an object with:
- `count`: number of movies in that genre
- `avgImdb`: average IMDB rating (rounded to 1 decimal)
- `titles`: array of movie titles in that genre

Since movies can have multiple genres, a movie may appear in multiple genre entries.

Example:
```
genreReport(movies)
// Returns: {
//   "drama": { count: 7, avgImdb: 8.9, titles: ["The Shawshank Exemption", ...] },
//   "crime": { count: 3, avgImdb: 8.9, titles: [...] },
//   ...
// }
```

exercises.solution:
function genreReport(movies) {
  const report = {};
  movies.forEach(movie => {
    movie.genres.forEach(genre => {
      if (!report[genre]) report[genre] = { count: 0, totalImdb: 0, titles: [] };
      report[genre].count++;
      report[genre].totalImdb += movie.ratings.imdb;
      report[genre].titles.push(movie.title);
    });
  });
  const result = {};
  for (const [genre, data] of Object.entries(report)) {
    result[genre] = {
      count: data.count,
      avgImdb: Math.round(data.totalImdb / data.count * 10) / 10,
      titles: data.titles
    };
  }
  return result;
}

