exercises.instructions:
Create a function called `movieAnalysis` that takes an array of movie objects and returns an analysis object with:
- `totalMovies`: total count of movies
- `avgRuntime`: average runtime rounded to nearest integer
- `topRated`: `{ title, rating }` of the movie with the highest IMDB rating
- `mostAwards`: `{ title, wins }` of the movie with the most award wins
- `genreBreakdown`: object mapping each genre to its count of movies

Example:
```
movieAnalysis(movies)
// Returns: {
//   totalMovies: 12,
//   avgRuntime: 144,
//   topRated: { title: "The Shawshank Exemption", rating: 9.3 },
//   mostAwards: { title: "Insheeption", wins: 157 },
//   genreBreakdown: { drama: 7, crime: 3, ... }
// }
```

exercises.solution:
function movieAnalysis(movies) {
  const totalMovies = movies.length;
  const avgRuntime = Math.round(movies.reduce((sum, m) => sum + m.runtime, 0) / movies.length);
  const topRatedMovie = movies.reduce((best, m) => m.ratings.imdb > best.ratings.imdb ? m : best);
  const mostAwardsMovie = movies.reduce((best, m) => m.awards.wins > best.awards.wins ? m : best);
  const genreBreakdown = {};
  movies.forEach(m => m.genres.forEach(g => { genreBreakdown[g] = (genreBreakdown[g] || 0) + 1; }));
  return {
    totalMovies,
    avgRuntime,
    topRated: { title: topRatedMovie.title, rating: topRatedMovie.ratings.imdb },
    mostAwards: { title: mostAwardsMovie.title, wins: mostAwardsMovie.awards.wins },
    genreBreakdown
  };
}

